{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-13T08:44:48.567Z",
  "steps": [
    "In an empty project the new recipe entry opens guidance, offers no invented actor, disables Create, and writes no author data.",
    "The ordinary World GUI creates an OC and then a compatible RPG player projection with size 72×88, speed 180 and blue color. Its source relationship points to that OC; no fixture author objects are injected.",
    "A delayed real catalog read disables creation while leaving Cancel available; cancellation plus late reply never reopens it or writes data. Full JSON review retains symbolic game-projection inheritance instead of flattening size/color/speed/controls. Chinese, English and Japanese at 390px retain fields/review, keep header and footer actions reachable, and allow source scrolling. Cancel changes neither author files nor editor state.",
    "Create transfers the reviewed JSON to a focused ordinary unsaved source draft without file writes. An external file occupying its path makes ordinary Save fail without overwrite, metadata registration, or draft loss; after removing only that owned test file, retry saves exactly the reviewed source and one registration. Earlier OC/projection bytes remain unchanged.",
    "The saved recipe immediately appears in scene preview with inherited 72×88 geometry, blue color and speed 180. Existing materialization creates a separate Scene2D preserving the same instance ID and useProjectionDefaults, with no serialized effective overrides and no modification of recipe or projection.",
    "Real Godot plan, build and headless run succeed for the GUI-authored chain. The inherited player moves 45px at speed 180 while preserving its scene instance identity. Plan/build/run change no author bytes."
  ],
